1. Subject

Telemetry Overlay (the "Software") is a work protected by copyright (French
Intellectual Property Code, books I and III) and by international treaties. The
Software includes, without limitation:
  - the source code and the published code, including in bundled, minified or
    otherwise transformed form;
  - the user interface: screen layout, sequence of functions, visual design,
    design of gauges, dials and instruments, texts, labels and messages;
  - the project's name and visual identity, logo, icons, images, screenshots,
    presentation videos, guide and documentation.

The fact that the Software is free of charge or that its files can be viewed
publicly grants no right other than those listed in section 2.

2. What is permitted

You may, free of charge:
  a) use the Software at its official address, currently
     https://tguillaume02.github.io/telemetry-overlay/ (or any address the
     author designates to replace it), including when
     installed from that address (web app), for personal or professional use;
  b) freely use the videos, images and files you produce with the Software
     from your own data: they belong to you;
  c) view the public repository and fork it on GitHub, only to the extent
     required by GitHub's Terms of Service. Such a fork grants no right to use,
     modify, publish or host the Software outside GitHub;
  d) take screenshots or short excerpts of the interface for an article,
     review, tutorial or video presenting the Software, naming it and giving
     its official address.

3. What is prohibited

Unless the author has given prior written permission, you may not, in whole or
in part, by any means:
  a) reproduce, copy, download in order to republish, distribute, sell, rent,
     lend, assign or sublicense the Software;
  b) host, upload, mirror or make the Software available at any address other
     than the official one, including on a local network or embedded in
     another website or application;
  c) modify, translate, adapt or arrange the Software, or create a derivative
     work from all or part of its code;
  d) reuse or imitate the Software's interface, visual design, gauge designs,
     logo or visual identity in another product;
  e) decompile, disassemble, "unminify" or analyse the Software's code to
     reconstruct its source code, except where expressly permitted by
     article L.122-6-1 of the French Intellectual Property Code;
  f) circumvent, disable or tamper with the Software's technical protection
     measures, including those restricting it to its official address;
  g) remove or alter copyright, licence or origin notices;
  h) extract the Software's code, texts or images by automated means (text
     and data mining), in particular to train or feed artificial intelligence
     models. The author expressly reserves this right within the meaning of
     article L.122-5-3 of the French Intellectual Property Code and article 4
     of Directive (EU) 2019/790.

4. Third-party components

Some components belong to third parties and remain under their own licence,
which prevails over this one for them:
  - the OSD fonts in fonts/osd/, from the fpv-wtf/msp-osd project, under the
    GNU GPL version 3 (file fonts/osd/LICENSE);
  - map and elevation tiles (Esri World Imagery, AWS Terrain Tiles), loaded
    from their servers and subject to their providers' terms.
The names and trademarks mentioned (DJI, GoPro, Insta360, Garmin, EdgeTX,
ArduPilot, INAV, Betaflight, Walksnail, etc.) belong to their respective owners
and are cited only to indicate compatibility.

5. Feedback

Suggestions, ideas and reports sent to the author (including through GitHub
issues) may be used freely by the author to improve the Software, without
compensation.

6. No warranty

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including accuracy of the displayed data, fitness for a particular
purpose or availability. To the extent permitted by law, the author shall not
be liable for any damage arising from the use of, or inability to use, the
Software. The Software must not be used for navigation, piloting or any safety
decision.

7. Termination

Any use contrary to this licence automatically terminates the rights it grants,
without prejudice to any action the author may take (including for copyright
infringement, articles L.335-2 et seq. of the French Intellectual Property
Code, or for unfair competition or free-riding).

8. Governing law

This licence is governed by French law. Any dispute falls under the competent
French courts, subject to mandatory consumer protection rules.

9. Permission requests

For any use not covered by section 2: https://github.com/tguillaume02
